   "promoted": "Promoted from 51 to the top of the 'next' block by Hidde on 2026-08-10, on Search Console evidence rather than on the demand proxy: /kyoto is the site's best-performing page by clicks (3 clicks on 34 impressions in the 10-day window, ahead of Lisbon's 2 on 48 and the homepage's 2 on 19). Demand ranking had it at 51 on 142,353 Wikipedia views; measured clicks beat the proxy whenever we have them.",
   "caveat": "What improving Kyoto can and cannot be. Its 10 trees span 35.5 km and NOT ONE has another within 2 km, the worst spread of any city on the site (CLAUDE.md's cluster doctrine names it as the counter-example to Cadiz). So Kyoto will never be an afternoon's walk, and adding trees to the existing ten would not change that. The work that pays is a genuine walkable cluster inside one district, Higashiyama or Arashiyama, which means researching a district rather than a city and accepting that the current ten stay a scattered list beside it. Photos are nearly done already: 8 of 10, missing only the Heian Cedar of Katanami and the Emperor's Gift Cherry of Kamigamo."
